.TH HARBORLENS 1 "Spiral Harbor" "Harbor Lens" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
harborlens \- measure software delivery and prepare records for Harbor Glass
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B harborlens assess
.I target
[\fB\-\-since\fR \fIDATE\fR]
[\fB\-\-until\fR \fIDATE\fR]
[\fB\-\-branch\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-deploy\-from\fR \fISOURCE\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIFMT\fR]
[\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.PP
.B harborlens export
.I target
[\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-push\-to\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
.B harborlens watch
[\fB\-\-bind\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-secret\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.PP
.B harborlens compare
.I target
[\fB\-\-cohort\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-baseline\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Harbor Lens reads the delivery history of a software team.
The free program prints all four DORA metrics.
Deployment frequency and lead time for changes are computed.
Time to restore service and change failure rate are printed and marked
not measured in the free tool.
Harbor Glass computes those two, plus incident linking, the model,
the benchmarks, and the recommendations.
The free report header states whether a GitHub token was found.
A token read from a file is reported as
.B found ./.env
(or the relative path of that file).
A token already set in the environment is reported as found there.
The header does not print the token.
This manual describes the full collector a subscriber runs.
The free program shipped in this repository implements
.B assess
only, and it counts git tags as deployments.
Options marked
.B Harbor Glass
are accepted by a subscriber build.
The free build prints an error for those options.
.PP
A change is a commit carried on a push event.
A deployment is a successful production release of one or more changes.
An incident is a closed issue that names the change which caused it.
The free build follows the view definitions in
.I queries/changes.sql
and
.IR queries/deployments.sql .
Incident rules are in
.I queries/incidents.sql
and are applied by Harbor Glass.
Bucket names follow
.IR METRICS.md .
The free build scores the span of the history you asked for.
The hosted dashboard scores the last three months from today.
.PP
.B assess
reads a local git repository, or clones a GitHub repository.
.B export
writes the same events as training records.
.B watch
receives live webhooks.
.B compare
places a result next to a Harbor Glass cohort.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B assess \fItarget\fR
Score a repository.
.I target
is a local path, a bare clone, or a GitHub URL of the form
https://github.com/owner/repo.
A URL is cloned with
.BR "git clone \-\-bare" .
A local path is read in place.
.TP
.B export \fItarget\fR
Write events_raw records for
.IR target .
This is the file a Harbor Glass training job consumes.
.B Harbor Glass
when combined with
.BR \-\-push\-to .
.TP
.B watch
Listen for GitHub, GitLab, and Cloud Build webhooks and append them
to the local event log.
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B compare \fItarget\fR
Print the four metrics and the distance from a named cohort.
.B Harbor Glass.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the Harbor Lens version and exit.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose
Print clone progress, rate-limit headers, and the deploy signal that
was chosen.
.TP
.B \-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet
Print only the four metric lines.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIFILE\fR
Read defaults from
.IR FILE .
The default path is
.IR ~/.config/harborlens/config.toml .
Command-line flags override the file.
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIFMT\fR
Report format.
.I FMT
is
.BR text ,
.BR json ,
or
.BR markdown .
The default is
.BR text .
.B markdown
is
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-since \fIDATE\fR
Ignore events before
.IR DATE .
Use YYYY-MM-DD.
.TP
.B \-\-until \fIDATE\fR
Ignore events after
.IR DATE .
Use YYYY-MM-DD.
.B Harbor Glass.
The free build scores through the latest event.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Do not call the GitHub API.
Git history and tags are still read.
A URL that is not already cached fails.
.SS assess
.TP
.B \-\-branch \fINAME\fR
Score the first parent of
.I NAME
instead of
.BR HEAD .
.TP
.B \-\-all\-branches
Include commits reachable from any branch head.
Deploy matching then uses topology instead of first-parent order.
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-deploy\-from \fISOURCE\fR
Where a deployment comes from.
.I SOURCE
is a comma-separated list of
.BR tags ,
.BR releases ,
.BR workflows ,
and
.BR deployments .
The free build accepts only
.BR tags .
The subscriber default is
.BR tags,releases,workflows,deployments ,
and the first source that yields events wins.
The report names the source it used.
.TP
.B \-\-workflow \fIGLOB\fR
When
.B \-\-deploy\-from
includes
.BR workflows ,
a successful run on the default branch counts as a deployment if the
workflow name matches
.IR GLOB .
Repeat the flag for more names.
Example:
.BR \-\-workflow "Redeploy*" .
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-environment \fINAME\fR
Keep deployments whose environment is
.IR NAME ,
such as
.B production
or
.BR preview .
Unmatched deployments are counted in a separate line and omitted from
the four metrics.
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-incident\-label \fINAME\fR
Label that marks an incident.
The free build always uses
.BR Incident .
A subscriber build may pass another name, or several by repeating
the flag.
.TP
.B \-\-root\-cause \fIREGEX\fR
Pattern that extracts the causing commit from an issue body.
The free build uses
.BR "root cause: <sha>" .
The pattern must contain one capture group.
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Store bare clones and API pages under
.IR DIR .
The default is
.IR .harborlens/
inside the current directory.
A second run reuses the cache.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Clone and fetch again, and do not write the cache.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-prs
Add pull-request timing to the report: time to first review, time to
merge, and median diff size.
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-actions
Add CI success rate and median duration for the default branch.
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-reviews
Add reviewer load and the share of reviews done by the busiest person.
.B Harbor Glass.
.SS export
.TP
.B \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
Write one JSON object per line.
Fields match the Four Keys
.B events_raw
table:
event_type, id, metadata, time_created, signature, msg_id, and source.
.B assess
accepts this flag as well.
.TP
.B \-\-push\-to \fIURL\fR
POST each event to the Four Keys webhook at
.IR URL ,
using the same signed headers as
.IR data\-generator/generate_data.py .
Requires
.B HARBOR_WEBHOOK_SECRET
or
.BR \-\-secret .
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
With
.BR \-\-push\-to ,
print the requests and send nothing.
.SS watch
.TP
.B \-\-bind \fIADDR\fR
Address and port to listen on.
The default is
.BR 127.0.0.1:8080 .
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-secret \fIFILE\fR
File containing the HMAC secret used to check
.B X\-Hub\-Signature
on incoming webhooks, and to sign
.B \-\-push\-to
requests.
.B Harbor Glass.
.SS compare
.TP
.B \-\-cohort \fINAME\fR
Benchmark cohort.
Built-in names are
.BR glass\-all ,
.BR glass\-startup ,
and
.BR glass\-regulated .
The report adds a band for each metric against that cohort.
.B Harbor Glass.
.TP
.B \-\-baseline \fIFILE\fR
Compare against a previous JSON report instead of a named cohort.
.B Harbor Glass.
.SH DEPLOYMENTS
The free build has one deploy signal.
Each git tag becomes a successful
.B deployment_status
event, which is what
.I queries/deployments.sql
counts for GitHub.
Annotated tags use the tagger date.
A lightweight tag has no tagger date, so the deploy time is the tagged
commit's timestamp.
That commit's own lead time is zero and is dropped.
Earlier commits in the release still count.
Tags that are not on the first parent of the selected branch are skipped.
A repository with no tags has no deployments.
That result is expected.
Many teams ship from a manually started workflow and never create a tag.
A subscriber build sees those runs when you pass
.B \-\-deploy\-from workflows
and a
.B \-\-workflow
pattern.
Releases and the GitHub Deployments API are the other subscriber sources.
.PP
Lead time is the median time from each included commit to the deployment
that contains it.
Zero minutes are ignored, matching
.IR METRICS.md .
.PP
The free report also prints time to restore service and change failure
rate, and marks both
.B not measured in the free tool.
A subscriber build computes them.
Time to restore and change failure rate are
.B Harbor Glass.
Time to restore is the median time from incident open, or from the
causing deployment if that is earlier, to incident close.
Change failure rate is the share of deployments linked to at least one
incident.
The bands are the same names
.I METRICS.md
uses for lead time, and 0-15%, 16-45%, or 46-60% for change failure.
A result of 0% means no deployment was linked to an incident.
It does not mean the service never failed.
.SH INCIDENTS
Harbor Glass keeps a closed issue only when a label is named exactly
.BR Incident .
The body line
.B root cause: <sha>
links that issue to a deployment.
The label
.B bug
does not count.
This is the rule in
.IR queries/incidents.sql .
The free build does not read issues, so a local repository and a GitHub
URL produce the same incident result: none.
The locked section of the free report names this analysis.
A subscriber build loads closed issues for a GitHub URL.
Pull requests on that list are skipped.
The first page holds 100 issues.
Further pages are fetched until the history in the requested window is
covered, which is why a larger repository needs
.BR GITHUB_TOKEN .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
Token sent when
.B assess
or
.B export
is given a GitHub URL.
Without it the API allows 60 requests per hour.
One free assessment uses one request.
A subscriber build pages until the history is exhausted and will spend
more of the quota.
With a token the limit is 5000 requests per hour.
A
.I .env
file in the working directory, or in a parent up through the git root,
may set
.BR GITHUB_TOKEN .
That is the recommended setup for a larger repository.
A value already in the environment overrides the file.
.TP
.B HARBOR_WEBHOOK
Default URL for
.BR \-\-push\-to .
.TP
.B HARBOR_WEBHOOK_SECRET
HMAC secret for
.B \-\-push\-to
when
.B \-\-secret
is omitted.
.TP
.B HARBORLENS_CONFIG
Overrides the default config file path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/harborlens/config.toml
Default configuration.
.TP
.I .env
Optional file of environment variables, including
.BR GITHUB_TOKEN .
Git ignores it.
.TP
.I .harborlens/
Cache of bare clones and API responses for the current directory.
.TP
.I harborlens/man/harborlens.1
This page, before it is installed onto the system man path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was written.
.TP
.B 1
The target was not a repository, git failed, or a Harbor Glass option
was passed to the free build.
.TP
.B 2
The GitHub API refused the request and
.B \-\-offline
was not set.
Cached history is still reported when it exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
Score a GitHub repository and keep the events:
.PP
.nf
.RS
export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_example
harborlens assess https://github.com/owner/repo
harborlens assess https://github.com/owner/repo \\
    --since 2025-01-01 --format json --output events.jsonl
.RE
.fi
.PP
Score a local checkout, including a bare clone:
.PP
.nf
.RS
harborlens assess .
harborlens assess /var/cache/repos/example.git --offline
.RE
.fi
.PP
A team that deploys by starting a workflow named Redeploy, and that
also deploys a preview environment.
These flags are
.BR "Harbor Glass" :
.PP
.nf
.RS
harborlens assess https://github.com/owner/repo \\
    --deploy-from workflows --workflow 'Redeploy' \\
    --environment production
harborlens assess https://github.com/owner/repo \\
    --deploy-from workflows --workflow 'Redeploy Preview' \\
    --environment preview
.RE
.fi
.PP
The same repository, using tags for production and ignoring a bot:
.PP
.nf
.RS
harborlens assess . --branch main --deploy-from tags \\
    --since 2024-06-01 --until 2025-06-01
.RE
.fi
.PP
Incidents stored under a company-specific label.
.B Harbor Glass:
.PP
.nf
.RS
harborlens assess https://github.com/owner/repo \\
    --incident-label sev1 --incident-label sev2 \\
    --root-cause 'caused by ([0-9a-f]{7,40})'
.RE
.fi
.PP
Write training records, then show the webhook body without sending it.
.B Harbor Glass
for the webhook:
.PP
.nf
.RS
harborlens export https://github.com/owner/repo --output train.jsonl
harborlens export . --push-to https://events.example.com/hook --dry-run
.RE
.fi
.PP
Receive webhooks on a laptop, then compare the default branch with the
startup cohort.
Both commands are
.BR "Harbor Glass" :
.PP
.nf
.RS
harborlens watch --bind 127.0.0.1:8088 --secret ./hook.secret
harborlens compare https://github.com/owner/repo --cohort glass-startup
harborlens compare . --baseline ./last-quarter.json
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
The free report prints all four DORA metrics.
Deployment frequency and lead time are computed.
Time to restore service and change failure rate are marked
not measured in the free tool.
The locked section names the Harbor Glass analyses that are not computed:
incidents, time to restore, change failure rate, reviewer load,
benchmarks, and a written improvement plan.
An incident is a closed issue labeled
.B Incident
whose body contains
.B root cause: <sha>.
The header says whether
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
was found, and never prints the token.
Running the subscriber flags against the free build is how a prospect
sees the boundary.
.PP
Install this page on Mac or Linux with the steps in
.IR HARBORLENS.md .
Windows has no
.B man
command.
There,
.B harborlens \-\-help
is the short reference, and the Windows Subsystem for Linux follows
the Linux install.
